## Lore

Octomen look like large walking octopi: eight tentacles on a small round torso, a bulbous head with two big eyes and a small beak. Four tentacles are legs, moving in a rolling rhythm, and four are arms dexterous enough to do anything a hand can. They are not sea creatures, and many cannot swim. Their rubbery skin runs red to brown and does not change color, and their voices are hoarse and rough.

The Splugorth found them about 500 years ago and, prizing their hardiness and dexterity, invaded their world; a few Shifters among them opened portals and saved some, but most went to the slave pits. In the market they fetch two or three times the price of comparable human slaves as Operators, mechanics and gunfighters. Octomen hate their enslavement, attack Splugorth Minions on slight provocation, and run an underground to free their kin; many have joined the Liberated Underground.

Free Octomen are mostly explorers and travellers, and many have reached Rifts Earth. They lean toward Wilderness Scouts and men at arms; a couple have become Cyber-Knights, and others roam as champions who hate tyrants and slavers. Evil ones become mercenaries, Gunslingers or criminals, and four arms make them superb gunfighters able to fire four revolvers at once. Their monstrous look frightens most people, and with no way to find others of their kind they feel very alone, which has made many gruff and impatient; good Octomen hide caring hearts and are loyal friends.

They prefer warm, dry climates, and many live in the New West. Escaped slaves are found in the Refuges and Preserves of Atlantis, in Africa and in southern Europe. They like humans and D-Bees and do not mind creatures of magic. They hate the Splugorth above all, and the Coalition kills them on sight.
', 'published', 'data-script'
